From: Andrey <17542208+osahv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:42:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Mesh: smaller node database entry (216 -> 152 bytes), 14
 nodes instead of 10

Sensor values are kept as small fixed-point numbers and positions as the 1e-7
degree integers they travel as, flags as bits, members ordered widest first.
Reading and writing a field looks exactly as before. Fourteen entries take less
memory than the ten did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
